      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The controlled change is a 10–20% relative enrichment of Ru while maintaining the nanoscale solid-solution structure.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ru enrichment promotes formation of partially oxidized Ru surface sites during ethanol oxidation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8392348::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The partially oxidized Ru sites remain embedded in the disordered PtPdRhRuIrOs alloy matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Composition-dependent local environments in complex solid solutions can modify local electronic structure and tune catalytic activity.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8048820::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial oxidation of enriched Ru shifts the Ru d-band center.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The electronic change at partially oxidized Ru modifies adsorption energies of ethanol-oxidation intermediates.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8048820::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified adsorption energetics facilitate oxidative removal of strongly bound CO-like intermediates.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Faster removal of strongly bound intermediates reduces catalyst poisoning.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A partially oxidized alloy surface can be more electrocatalytically active than its component metals.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8392348::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ru enrichment will lower the ethanol-oxidation onset potential relative to the equiatomic catalyst.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ru enrichment will increase ethanol-oxidation current density relative to the equiatomic catalyst.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8392348::webcard",
        "PMC8048820::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ru enrichment will reduce CO adsorption or poisoning relative to the equiatomic catalyst.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ru enrichment will improve current retention during durability cycling relative to the equiatomic catalyst.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed effects should hold within the usual ethanol-oxidation potential window and electrolyte conditions, provided the solid-solution structure is retained.",
